    {
      "contentTypeKey": "458004c2-2f2b-40bf-8fd7-cad968995e49",
      "key": "20413ff0-26c5-4a9b-b8e1-d994a3d95642",
      "values": []
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "34e5aa3b-db10-40a1-893d-79e98cd3f2f4",
      "key": "b171c8f6-e91b-43fc-a289-5ad87d2918b9",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Features"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHalf board accommodation\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll excursions \u0026amp; guided tours included\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBlue Badge guide Days 2 to 4\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EExecutive coach throughout\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOne free place per 10 paying passengers\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "1d09b5af-b95a-4af5-b8f2-323db029e817",
      "key": "b144b4ea-99dd-4d8c-8201-47c35deffba6",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Accommodation"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EFour nights on half board basis at the 3* Gibside Hotel at Whickham, four miles south west of Newcastle. Facilities include a restaurant and bar. All rooms are en suite.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "2d9b0603-29ef-423a-8d3e-d9c039d3d7b1",
      "key": "6c3ea8c1-416f-46e9-964a-2be09a066bd1",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHarewood House, Yorkshire\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EDurham Cathedral - guided tour\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ELaing Art Gallery\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAlnwick Castle\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECragside House \u0026amp; Gardens\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ELindisfarne Castle\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBoat trip to Farne Island\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Bowes Museum - guided tour\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "de535189-b468-4594-8118-f303bac50e3c",
      "key": "e91299ab-73c0-451a-afa4-ed05a0114ff0",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Tailor your sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHadrian\u2019s Wall Country - a tour of this World Heritage Site dating back to 122 AD takes in Chester\u2019s Roman Fort, one of the best preserved examples of a Roman cavalry fort in Britain, and Cawfields Roman Wall, one of the best preserved and most scenic stretches with turrets and an impressive milecastle thought to have been built by the Second Legion\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHexham Abbey - a church was originally established on this site in 674AD, while the current Early English style building dates from the 12th century\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWallington House, Morpeth - dating from 1688, the house contains magnificent Rococo plasterwork, fine ceramics and a collection of dolls\u2019 houses\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBelsay Hall, Castle \u0026amp; Gardens, Morpeth - a fine medieval castle enlarged into a Jacobean mansion, while Belsay Hall is a Greek Revival villa with its fabulous Pillar Hall and the huge grounds feature the unique Quarry Garden\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWashington Old Hall - the original medieval home of George Washington\u0027s ancestors, from where the family took their surname of \u0027Washington\u0027\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESpanish Gallery, Bishop Auckland - depicts a story of Golden Age Spanish art during the 16th and 17th centuries\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Here are some more suggested places of interest you might like to include:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "837beecf-4239-4b3d-b683-1d611af3da2e",
      "key": "126a7061-b96e-4815-a2af-ef3a97c7c5ce",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch3\u003EDay 1 \u2013 Harewood House\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EBoard our private executive coach at your preferred pick up points \u2013 stop at a convenient property en route such as Harewood House, the home of the Queen\u2019s cousin, the Earl of Harewood, renowned for its stunning architecture, fine art collection, exquisite Adam interiors and Chippendale furniture and a 1,000 acre \u2018Capability\u2019 Brown landscaped garden - continue to the 3* Gibside Hotel at Whickham.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 2 \u2013 Durham Cathedral \u0026amp; Laing Art Gallery\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ETour with our Blue Badge guide of Durham and its Cathedral, once described as \u2018one of the great architectural experiences of Europe\u2019 \u2013 Laing Art Gallery in Newcastle boasts an exceptional collection focusing on British oil paintings, watercolours, ceramics, silver and glassware.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 3 \u2013 Alnwick Castle \u0026amp; Cragside House and Gardens\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EOur Blue Badge guide accompanies us to Alnwick Castle, the second largest inhabited castle in England after Windsor Castle and home of the Earls and Dukes of Northumberland since 1309 \u2013 the National Trust\u2019s Cragside House and Gardens, a wonderful Victorian mansion dating from the 19th century and described as \u2018the palace of a modern magician\u2019, features what were then state of the art hydraulics powering a revolutionary lift system and internal telephones which mesmerised visitors in its time.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 4 \u2013 Lindisfarne Priory \u0026amp; Farne Island\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ESettled by Irish monks in AD 635, Lindisfarne Priory, also known as Holy Island, became the hub of a major cult celebrating the achievements of St Cuthbert (c634-687) and the famous Lindisfarne Gospels were created in his honour on the island in the early 8th century \u2013 boat trip to Farne Island, one of Britain\u2019s most important bird sanctuaries and home to puffins, eider duck and four species of tern.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 5 \u2013 The Bowes Museum\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EGuided tour of The Bowes Museum at Barnard Castle, a purpose built public art gallery created by John and Josephine Bowes between 1862 and 1875 and home to a large collection of fine and decorative paintings from around Europe \u2013 return to our original departure points with comfort stops en route.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Suggested Itinerary"
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Every one of our tours is exclusively for your group and your group alone so each one can be tailor made to suit the interests and profile of your members until you have a tour with an itinerary and at a price which matches the interests and profile of your members."
        },
